@ 47.2 - List 2: Conditional or complex consonant changes
# citation: Western and Eastern Armenian often have swapped voicing in stop consonants: e.g.
# 			vardapet vs. vartabed. This is a result of changes related to aspiration.
	w > f
	m > n / _i
	{t,k} > ∅ / V_V
	p > w / V_V
	b d ɡ > b:[+ long] d:[+ long] ɡ:[+ long] / V_V
	t > k / _s̩
	n > i / _s